note How the tool reaches version control: jj when a .jj directory is at or above the root, else git when a .git is, so a repo colocated with git is jj's. Only through the command line, never a library. Two questions are asked of it: the map at the parent revision, for diff, and one source file at a revision, for repin. The parent is @- in jj and HEAD in git.

